// MT2003 positive-fire: a `let` binding without a type annotation whose
// initializer is an empty array literal `[]`. The element type cannot be
// inferred from local information. Pre-v0.14 (Gap B / KNOWN_ISSUES #11)
// the type checker silently kept the element type as a free inference
// variable, defaulted it to the Error sentinel at the end of the body,
// and any downstream use surfaced as a less helpful trap. v0.14 (Gap B
// / MT2003 emit-site) detects the empty-container shape inside
// `check_stmt(HirStmt::Let)` and fires MT2003 with the binding name.
//
// Spec ref: §7.2 (inference) of v1.0-RC2; KNOWN_ISSUES #11 v1.x
// emit-landing plan (trait-iterator + collect chain row).
fn main() -> I32 {
  let xs = []
  42
}
